// The stills, and everything else that has a capacity or a service
// interval.
//
// Bulk containers are vessels that hold alcohol, and they were already
// first-class. What never existed is the plant: the still itself, the
// mash tun, the filler, the pumps — things a run is performed *on*
// rather than *into*. Without them a distillation run names no still,
// capacity is a number in somebody's head, and maintenance is a reminder
// on a phone.
//
// Where a figure has not been recorded it is absent rather than zero, and
// what depends on it refuses rather than assuming. A made-up run duration
// produces a schedule that looks authoritative and is fiction.

